ASPIRATIONAL — FIXED-CHAR store column `char[N]`. NOT built yet. Tier A of strings.

Surface (blessed with Lars 2026-07-21):
  - `label: char[16]` — fixed-length byte column; SoA `[CAP][16]u8`. Static,
    zero-alloc, NO ownership (the take/discharge tier is variable-strings, LATER).
  - write: `stored/insert { ...label: "buy milk" }` — string literal copies into
    the buffer. Overflow: compile-error if a comptime-known literal exceeds N;
    otherwise runtime-truncate (a `| toolong` branch mirroring `| full` is a
    possible refinement, deferred).
  - read/print: `query { entity.label }` binds a string; `{{ label:s }}` prints,
    trimmed at first NUL.
  - Rides 690_049's typed-column emission — char[N] extends field_types to an
    array-of-bytes type. i64/f64 columns coexist unchanged.

Expected once built: `[0] buy milk` / `[1] ship koru`.
